        <section id="recursions"  class="t-bg-primary">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Recursions
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>Recursion is when an entity such as a function calls back to itself. It is often controlled externally through means such as iterations in a list.</p>
<p>Recursion used to solve complex problems by breaking them down into simpler ones or smaller instances of the same problem, until we reach a defined base state.</p>
<p>It is often used as an alternative to iteration which can be written through simpler, though not always as computationally efficient, code.</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/uc/uc_u2_s2_p5_image.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </section>
        
    
     
    
  
     
    
  
  
        <section id="recursion-example" >
          
            <h2>Recursion example</h2>
              <p>Here is a recursive function in Python. The function will take a list of integers and a threshold.</p>
<p>If the sum of the list of integers is larger than the threshold, the list is shortened by one value (the first value – an example of First In First Out). It then calls itself (this is the recursion) until the base state is reached.</p>
<p>We have 2 criteria here for the base state: either</p>
<ol>
<li>there are only 2 values in the remaining list, or</li>
<li>the sum of the remaining values in the list is less than the threshold.</li>
</ol>
<p>You can try changing the threshold or the list indexes to get different answers.</p>

              
              <div class="c-code"><pre class="language-python"><code class="language-python"><span class="highlight-line"><span class="token comment"># Define a recursive function</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line"><span class="token keyword">def</span> <span class="token function">sum_of_list_below</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>input_list<span class="token punctuation">,</span> threshold_value<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line"></span><br><span class="highlight-line">    list_sum <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token builtin">sum</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>input_list<span class="token punctuation">)</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line"></span><br><span class="highlight-line">    <span class="token comment"># Base state 1: more than 2 values in list</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line">    <span class="token keyword">if</span> <span class="token builtin">len</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>input_list<span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token operator">&lt;</span> <span class="token number">3</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line">        <span class="token keyword">print</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'Threshold not reached'</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line">        <span class="token keyword">return</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line">    </span><br><span class="highlight-line">    <span class="token comment"># Base state 2: list sum is below threshold</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line">    <span class="token keyword">if</span> list_sum <span class="token operator">></span> threshold_value<span class="token punctuation">:</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line">      input_list <span class="token operator">=</span> input_list<span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token number">1</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span><span class="token builtin">len</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>input_list<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token operator">-</span><span class="token number">1</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line"></span><br><span class="highlight-line">      <span class="token comment"># Here is the recursive function call</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line">      sum_of_list_below<span class="token punctuation">(</span>input_list<span class="token punctuation">,</span> threshold_value<span class="token punctuation">)</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line">    <span class="token keyword">else</span><span class="token punctuation">:</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line">      <span class="token keyword">print</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'Reached threshold at list length'</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token builtin">len</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>input_list<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line">      <span class="token keyword">print</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'List: '</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> input_list<span class="token punctuation">)</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line">      <span class="token keyword">print</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'List sum: '</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> list_sum<span class="token punctuation">)</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line"></span><br><span class="highlight-line"><span class="token comment"># Define a list of numbers</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line">list_1 <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token number">1</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token number">5</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token number">6</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token number">5</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token number">7</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token number">3</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token number">7</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token number">3</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token number">2</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line"></span><br><span class="highlight-line"><span class="token comment"># Define a threshold</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line">threshold <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token number">20</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line"></span><br><span class="highlight-line"><span class="token comment"># Call the recursive function</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line">sum_of_list_below<span class="token punctuation">(</span>list_1<span class="token punctuation">,</span> threshold<span class="token punctuation">)</span></span></code></pre>
</div>

            
          
        </section>
        
    
     
    
  
  
        <section id="result" >
          
            <h2>Result</h2>
              <p>In this example, we can see that the threshold was reached when it got to the middle 3 values in the list (5, 7, and 3).</p>

              
              <div class="c-code"><pre class="language-text"><code class="language-text"><span class="highlight-line">Reached threshold at list length 3</span><br><span class="highlight-line">List: [5, 7, 3]</span><br><span class="highlight-line">List sum: 15</span></code></pre>
</div>

            
              <p>Recursive constructs are often used in algorithms and most programming languages implement recursion by allowing a function to call itself. However, if the base state is incorrectly defined, infinite loops can occur that may cause can crash the system as it balloons out of control.</p>

          
        </section>
        
    
     
    
  
     
    
  
  
